# SINT with a data file shorter than its header (PLAN 1.4b, 2026-10-23).  SetIntSrf counted the row
# its READ hit END on, so a header declaring more points than the file holds kept one UNREAD row of
# its local SURFACE array as a data point: on the f = 1 m paraboloid of tst_trace_rewrites.in with a
# 1e-6 piston + 1e-4 r^2 deviation on 225 points, a header of 226 (or 255) moved the focal-plane OPD
# from RMS 5.6306e-7 / P-V 1.906e-6 to 6.170e-7 / 4.128e-6 (gfortran) or 6.157e-7 / 3.837e-6 (ifx:
# the phantom row is whatever the stack held), silently.  Now the rows read are used, with a warning
# naming the counts (the short file stays tolerated: guards warn); fewer than 3 read is "Too few".
# Legs: the exact file, then the 226- and 255-point headers -- each traces as the exact file; then the
# exact file under the bindings' spelling, the deck name without its '.in' (tst_trace_rewrites.srf1.txt):
# the CLI tries its own spelling first, names it missing, and reads the other (the api's SMACOS filnam
# drops '.in', so before this each front end found only its own spelling -- and SMACOS then looped on
# its prompt, re-reading 'SINT' from its stack forever).
# COPY: $ROOT/ZGD_test_files/tst_trace_rewrites.in
cd $TMP
old $DECK
none
! awk 'BEGIN{print 225,1;for(i=-7;i<=7;i++)for(j=-7;j<=7;j++){x=i*0.0175;y=j*0.0175;printf "%g %g %.12g\n",x,y,1e-6+1e-4*(x*x+y*y)}}' > tst_trace_rewrites.in.srf1.txt
sint
opd 2
! awk 'BEGIN{print 226,1;for(i=-7;i<=7;i++)for(j=-7;j<=7;j++){x=i*0.0175;y=j*0.0175;printf "%g %g %.12g\n",x,y,1e-6+1e-4*(x*x+y*y)}}' > tst_trace_rewrites.in.srf1.txt
sint
opd 2
! awk 'BEGIN{print 255,1;for(i=-7;i<=7;i++)for(j=-7;j<=7;j++){x=i*0.0175;y=j*0.0175;printf "%g %g %.12g\n",x,y,1e-6+1e-4*(x*x+y*y)}}' > tst_trace_rewrites.in.srf1.txt
sint
opd 2
! rm tst_trace_rewrites.in.srf1.txt; awk 'BEGIN{print 225,1;for(i=-7;i<=7;i++)for(j=-7;j<=7;j++){x=i*0.0175;y=j*0.0175;printf "%g %g %.12g\n",x,y,1e-6+1e-4*(x*x+y*y)}}' > tst_trace_rewrites.srf1.txt
sint
opd 2
# EXPECT: File \S*tst_trace_rewrites\.in\.srf1\.txt does not exist\.\s+Compute time was[\s\S]*?RMS OPD error is   5\.6305\d+D-07 m\s+P-V OPD error is   1\.9064\d+D-06 m
# EXPECT: MACOS> sint\s+Computing interpolated surface data\.\.\.\s+Compute time was[\s\S]*?RMS OPD error is   5\.6305\d+D-07 m\s+P-V OPD error is   1\.9064\d+D-06 m
# EXPECT: \*\* Interpolated surface data, element   1: \S*tst_trace_rewrites\.in\.srf1\.txt declares 226 points, 225 read; the points read are used[\s\S]*?RMS OPD error is   5\.6305\d+D-07 m\s+P-V OPD error is   1\.9064\d+D-06 m
# EXPECT: \*\* Interpolated surface data, element   1: \S*tst_trace_rewrites\.in\.srf1\.txt declares 255 points, 225 read; the points read are used[\s\S]*?RMS OPD error is   5\.6305\d+D-07 m\s+P-V OPD error is   1\.9064\d+D-06 m
# EXPECT-NOT: not correctly set
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
